<title>UK: Shield gains as finance director ups stake.</title>
<headline>Shield gains as finance director ups stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Shield Diagnostics Plc rebounded from recent weakness on Thursday as the company said finance director David Evans had doubled his holding in the company with the purchase of 8,500 shares.</p>
<p>The stock was up 7p at 117-1/2 by 1349 GMT, after yesterday closing at their lowest level in a year.</p>
<p>Earlier this month Shield said it fell to a pre-tax loss of 291,100 stg in the six months ended September 30 from a profit of 43,600 stg a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
